    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Cleopatra inherited in 51 BCE a kingdom indebted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, lost a civil war to her brother Ptolemy XIII, and was restored by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> in 47 BCE.</li><li>With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> she regained former Ptolemaic lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> and Cyrene, and in 34 BCE the Donations of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> named her children rulers of the east.</li><li>Octavian declared war on her, won at Actium in 31 BCE and invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 30 BCE; she killed herself, and Egypt became a Roman province.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papyrus">papyrus</a> of 33 BCE granting tax exemptions to a Roman ends, in a different hand, with the Greek word for &quot;make it happen&quot;; it is possibly Cleopatra's own autograph.</p></aside>
    </section>

